          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "K.R.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.428,
            0.282,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "India’s atmospheric scientist, climbed to an"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.311,
            0.361,
            0.89,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "in temperature with height in the stratosphere calms the layer due to the lack of vertical mixing of air, keeping weather confined to the troposphere. Above the stratosphere are the mesosphere, thermosphere and exosphere, but they play only a minor role in regulating climate on the surface of the Earth. At about 100 km above the Earth is the start of the region, we call the outer space. These atmospheric layers show how the atmosphere regulates energy flow, shaping weather, climate and life."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.075,
            0.489,
            0.278,
            0.69
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "altitude of 18,000 feet in the Himalayas in 1934 to measure the ozone levels, and discovered that they were lower than expected. His work laid the foundation for understanding how UV absorption varies with altitude and pollution. Later on, he led early monsoon forecasting efforts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.524,
            0.885,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_caption",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.434,
                0.503,
                0.767,
                0.521
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Table 13.2: Key atmospheric layers"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.318,
                0.524,
